window.products.push({"id":86175,"name":"Thermador 48 In. Stainless Steel Gas Range - PRG486JDG","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71kc2kyfu4L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"The combination of powerful performance and elegant styling makes the Thermador Professional Series Range the epitome of American luxury in the kitchen. With ultimate performance driven innovation, these ranges now feature our easy-to-clean porcelain cooktop, ExtraLow simmering featuring our Star Burners, 22,000 BTUs Power Burner, a large capacity Convection Oven and SoftClose doors.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71kc2kyfu4L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Thermador","source_asin":"B005LYRKQW","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-86175","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B005LYRKQW","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B005LYRKQW","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":86176,"name":"2198202 Thermostat for Whirlpool Refrigerator WP2198202 Cold Control Temperature Kenmore Part AP6006166 PS11739232 Assembly 106.55642500 ED2VHEXVB01 E","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":9.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61yiikCjrvS._SL1488_.jpg","description":"💡 Whirlpool Thermostat 2198202 - An equivalent for parts 1110552, 1115242, 1115243, 1115244, 1115245, 1129437, 2161283, 2161284, 2169112, 2169113, 2198201, 2299, 99989726, WP2198202VP. Thermostat Wp2198202 is compatible with Whirlpool, Amana, Crosley, Estate, Inglis, Kenmore, KitchenAid, Maytag, Roper appliances. The thermostat works as a sensor in refrigerator units and freezers. It senses temperature changes in the evaporator during the defrost cycle and switches off when the ice has melted. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Ultra Durable 2198202 Refrigerator Cold Control will help if your appliance doesn't start, fridge or freezer are too warm / too cold. To complete this repair project, you will need specific tools - a putty knife, Phillips and flat blade screwdriver, 1/4 inch nut driver, and needle nose pliers. 💡 Kenmore Refrigerator Thermostat Wp2198202, also known as the defrost bi-metal thermostat, is an essential component of a refrigerator's defrost system. The primary function of the Whirlpool Refrigerator Thermostat Wp2198202 is to regulate the temperature in the freezer and prevent ice build-up on the evaporator coil. Temperature Control Thermostat Wp2198202 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 The Wp2198202 Thermostat is designed to operate at a specific temperature range, typically between 0°F and 50°F (-17°C and 10°C). If the thermostat is defective, it can cause the defrost heater to either stay on or not turn on at all, leading to excessive frost build-up on the evaporator coil. This can cause the refrigerator to become less efficient and may eventually lead to other problems such as water leaking onto the floor or spoiled food. 💡 How does the thermostat works? Whirlpool Wp2198202 Defrost Thermostat is made of two different metals that expand and contract at different rates in response to temperature changes. When the temperature drops below a certain point, the metal inside the thermostat contracts, causing the contacts inside to close and completing the circuit that activates the defrost heater. Once the temperature rises again, the metal expands, causing the contacts to open and stopping the defrost cycle.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61yiikCjrvS._SL1488_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07VW7SLLJ","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-86176","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07VW7SLLJ","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07VW7SLLJ","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
